    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1fc329554022abfab5e77f6c7bf5f34d36491d7ed3e34ac4030dcbf768434845",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The exact finite phase count supplies a regulator-conditioned account of the smooth Riemann term: its continuum limit is a finite deficit in a divergent spectrum, interpreted as interaction-induced blueshift from a fixed energy window; its renormalized transfer product yields the Gamma phase; a zeta-regularization scale supplies the otherwise missing linear coefficient; and a half-unit offset improves the retrospective alignment of the smooth count with known zero ordinates.",
