    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2e13bc5af0d48d919175822a0458940308a4507022b1611a655243c024264736",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses failed level-list modifications to diagnose a representation bottleneck: sums of smooth arctangent phase steps can change coarse density without readily generating zero-scale irregularity. It then promotes the formerly boundary-like g coupling into the dynamics, where RG closure restricts a generic symmetric coupling matrix to two directional max/min patterns; after continuum integration, the gradients of their running couplings become opposite-sign local scattering potentials.",
