    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_998013d52638d47fb69f97659bd5e83f4bb422b77472ae805aad7e7509e3e0b8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The adapted coordinate q(n)=integral_1^n dn'/epsilon(n') turns the continuum spectral problem into free phase propagation on a finite interval with a coupling-controlled boundary twist, while the complementary coordinate s(n)=L_N-q(n) measures progress under elimination. In that same adapted length, the state-conditioned coupling follows a cycle; removing one cycle from the quantization integral lowers the spectral label by one, and the label counts completed cycles to leading order.",
